    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-efficiency matchup of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.49), who benefits from an optimal hitting environment and a favorable 4.37 xERA matchup against Fisher. His dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) makes him our primary offensive engine. Joining him at the top of the production hierarchy is **Drake Baldwin** (68.73), whose move into the #2 spot provides a significant +8% order bonus. While **Sam Antonacci** (62.70) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.36) both clear the 60-point threshold for strong starts, the latter gains a specific advantage from the slow delivery of Fisher, which historically inflates SB opportunity for our speed-first strategy. \n\nStrategic tension remains in the lower half of our order, where the optimizer prioritized **Wade Meckler** (54.93) over the marginal options due to an elite +19% SP skill adjustment against the hittable Dobnak. Conversely, **Andy Pages** (46.78) serves as the day\u2019s greatest risk; while his #3 spot suggests volume, he faces an elite arm in Misiorowski (2.03 xERA), significantly suppressing his ceiling. The toughest bench decision involved **Liam Hicks** (48.67), who technically cleared the \"marginal\" floor but was ultimately relegated to the bench in favor of more efficient platoon alignments. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the bench due to an assumed non-start, while **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** continue to hold up our progress from the IL, leaving the active roster to carry the load. \n\nLooking ahead, we must navigate the platoon disadvantages facing **Gunnar Henderson** (42.45) and **Nasim Nunez** (43.24). Both players are suffering from negative SP skill impacts and unfavorable platoon splits today, putting them dangerously close to our \"Below Floor\" threshold. Unless **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, or **Luis Lara** find their way into the defensive rotation for their respective clubs, we are effectively locked into this configuration. The primary risk today is the performance of **Gunnar Henderson** against Seymour, where the -15% dynamic platoon hit is compounded by the pitcher\u2019s stinginess, making this a pivotal game for our overall Roto standing.",
